    <extension point="xbmc.python.pluginsource" library="resources/lib/default.py">
        <provides>video</provides>
    </extension>
    <extension point="xbmc.service" library="resources/lib/service.py"/>
    <extension point="kodi.context.item">
        <menu id="kodi.core.main">
            <item library="resources/lib/context_restart.py">
                <label>30909</label>
                <visible>[Window.IsVisible(tvguide) | Window.IsVisible(pvrchannelguide)] + ListItem.InProgress + ListItem.IsPlayable</visible>
            </item>
            <menu>
                <label>PseudoTV Live</label>
                <item library="resources/lib/context_record.py" args="add">
                    <label>30115</label>
                    <visible>[String.Contains(ListItem.Plot,"item=") + ListItem.HasEpg] + [Window.IsVisible(tvguide)|Window.IsVisible(tvsearch)|Window.IsVisible(tvchannels)]</visible>
                </item>
                <item library="resources/lib/context_record.py" args="del">
                    <label>30117</label>
                    <visible>[String.StartsWith(ListItem.PVRInstanceName, PseudoTV Live) + Window.IsVisible(tvrecordings)]</visible>
                </item>
                <item library="resources/lib/default.py" args="?mode=playlist">
                    <label>30076</label>
                    <visible>[String.Contains(ListItem.Plot,"item=") + ListItem.HasEpg] + [Window.IsVisible(tvguide)|Window.IsVisible(tvsearch)|Window.IsVisible(tvchannels)]</visible>
                </item>
                <item library="resources/lib/context_info.py" args="info">
                    <label>30075</label>
                    <visible>[String.Contains(ListItem.Plot,"item=") + ListItem.HasEpg] + [Window.IsVisible(tvguide)|Window.IsVisible(tvsearch)|Window.IsVisible(tvchannels)]</visible>
                </item>
                <item library="resources/lib/context_info.py" args="match">
                    <label>30091</label>
                    <visible>[String.Contains(ListItem.Plot,"item=") + ListItem.HasEpg] + [Window.IsVisible(tvguide)|Window.IsVisible(tvsearch)|Window.IsVisible(tvchannels)]</visible>
                </item>
                <item library="resources/lib/context_info.py" args="browse">
                    <label>30087</label>
                    <visible>[String.Contains(ListItem.Plot,"item=") + ListItem.HasEpg] + [Window.IsVisible(tvguide)|Window.IsVisible(tvsearch)|Window.IsVisible(tvchannels)]</visible>
                </item>
                <item library="resources/lib/context_create.py" args="add">
                    <label>30114</label>
                    <visible>[!ListItem.IsPlayable + ListItem.IsFolder] + [!String.IsEmpty(ListItem.Label)]</visible>
                </item>
                <item library="resources/lib/context_create.py" args="open_manager">
                    <label>32261</label>
                    <visible>[String.Contains(ListItem.Plot,"item=")]</visible>
                </item>
                <item library="resources/lib/context_create.py" args="open_manager">
                    <label>30107</label>
                    <visible>[!String.Contains(ListItem.Plot,"item=")]</visible>
                </item>
            </menu>
        </menu>
    </extension>
    <extension point="xbmc.addon.metadata">
        <summary lang="en_GB">PseudoTV Live with M3U/XMLTV live import support.</summary>
        <description lang="en_GB">Fork variant of PseudoTV Live (madteevee) that adds live channel imports from external M3U + XMLTV sources (local files or HTTP URLs) with conflict-cascade allocation and per-channel operator overrides. Designed for parallel install alongside the standard PseudoTV Live addon.</description>
        <platform>all</platform>
        <license>GPL-3.0-or-later</license>
        <source>https://github.com/PseudoTV/PseudoTV_Live</source>
        <forum>https://forum.kodi.tv/showthread.php?tid=355549</forum>
        <disclaimer lang="en_GB">BETA PROJECT; SUBJECT TO BUGS</disclaimer>
        <news>v0.8.0+imports.63
- Fixed: rebuilding one of your own channels no longer replaces a show that has already started; the new line-up begins when the show on now ends.
- Fixed: "Play programme" in the TV guide menu on a show that is on now joins it part-way through (when the guide passes the show's times) and no longer fails to play.
- Fixed: the "Up next" time is right (it was an hour early, two in summer), and guide times stay right across the change to and from summer time.
- Changed: past shows leave the guide exactly "Minimum (Past) Guide Days" after they end (an hour sooner than before).
- Changed: the RESTART button appears as soon as Kodi's channel banner goes away (about 5 seconds sooner).
v0.8.0+imports.62
- New: restart a show that is already running from its beginning, on your own channels and on LiveTV channels that can replay it (Movistar+): a RESTART button after you tune in, "Restart from beginning" in the TV guide menu, and a remote button you set up (NotifyAll(pseudotv,restart)).
- Changed: "Restart Percentage" starts at 5% on new installs (was 95%); existing installs keep their value: set it in Settings, Global, Overlay.
- Fixed: the RESTART button never appeared, and the channel rule "Restart Button" switched it off after the first stop.</news>
        <reuselanguageinvoker>true</reuselanguageinvoker>
